{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And they hated him yet more for his dreams and for his words.</b> He explains that the hatred they bore him was for two things: one, for the dream he dreamed, and the second, for the telling, which he would recount to them and boast in it, like one who has done a righteous deed, saying to them, 'Hear, pray, this dream which I have dreamed.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:10.185478127Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}